;Purpose: PyTorch from plain MeTTa through py-call: tensors, algebra,
;  reductions, activations, the exits back to MeTTa data and autograd, with no
;  Python-side setup needed beyond torch being importable.
;Generated by: extensions/python/tools/facegen.py --write; edit this header, never the body
;Import: from torch import tensor, zeros, ones, randn, arange, matmul, add, sub, mul, div, sum, mean, relu, sigmoid
;Import: from torch.Tensor import item, tolist, shape, requires_grad_, backward, grad
;Signature: relu(input) -> Tensor
;Signature: arange(end) -> Tensor
;Signature: arange(start, end) -> Tensor
;Signature: arange(start, end, step) -> Tensor
;Effect: randn oracleIO  random construction, which a signature shows as an ordinary constructor
;Effect: item readOnlyLookup  the docstring's return is the word "number", which names no type
;Effect: tolist readOnlyLookup  the docstring's return is the words "list or number", which name no type
;Read from: torch 2.13.0+cpu
;
;A head is the import's module prefix and the name's own spelling with
;underscores read as hyphens. Each declaration is one reachable POSITIONAL call
;form: a defaulted parameter makes its arity optional, a `*args` serves zero to
;four arguments, and `**kwargs` and keyword-only parameters are absent, because
;a MeTTa call site passes positionally. A parameter the module does not annotate
;is `%Undefined%`, and so is every foreign class: a py-call'd object's type IS
;`%Undefined%`, and a face naming the class would refuse the call it wraps. The
;effect class inside each arrow is derived from the result the signature
;declares -- a scalar or a container answers a VALUE and is `readOnlyLookup`, a
;live foreign object or a call made for what it does is `writesState`, and a
;result nothing declares is `oracleIO`, the top, exactly as the engine
;classifies `py-call` itself -- and an `Effect:` line above declares the review
;a signature cannot show.

(: torch-tensor (-[det,writesState]-> %Undefined% %Undefined%))
(@doc torch-tensor (@kind function) (@desc "Constructs a tensor with no autograd history (also known as a \"leaf tensor\", see :doc:`/notes/autograd`) by copying :attr:`data`.") (@params ((@param (@type %Undefined%) (@desc "Initial data for the tensor. Can be a list, tuple, NumPy ``ndarray``, scalar, and other types.")))) (@return (@type %Undefined%) (@desc "")))
(= (torch-tensor $data) (py-call (torch.tensor $data)))

